message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Strange loop in J-space: a self-description that changes its own reading"
authors:
  - family-names: Tomasik
    given-names: Wiktor
date-released: 2026-10-19
version: "4.0"
url: "https://github.com/Pixedar/jspace-strange-loop"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Pixedar/jspace-strange-loop"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
keywords:
  - self-modeling
  - strange loop
  - language models
  - attention
  - representation geometry
  - multimodal models
abstract: >-
  A small self-describing attention loop around a frozen language model. Removing a destination
  shortcut from field discrimination can produce state-dependent movement from organized starts.
  Path interventions locate that dependence mainly in the reader. A shared spotlight changes
  the language model's predictions, while the measured return through model processing remains
  weak. Field pattern agreement does not establish calibrated forecasts, useful online prediction,
  persistent individuality or subjective experience. Earlier frozen feedback, chunked reasoning,
  evidence selection and negative causal-map results are preserved as distinct research branches.
